- op: discuss  # 8a69
  at: '2026-11-01T07:56:28Z'  # 8a69
  by: agent  # 8a69
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8a69
  clock: 4  # 8a69
  nonce: 8a69  # 8a69
  message: "Fixed in PR #1985 (merged to dev 6afecacb1b). Root cause: puppet.py read a class name as one bare identifier, so `class a::b` was never extracted, and it read only the first name of an include, so `include a::b, c` and `include \"c\"` dropped names; includes of existing classes stayed unbound in any order. Fix: _class_names reads every name an include / require-function / inherits writes (lists, quoted, ::-prefixed); class definitions keep their full namespaced name; `require x` gives an includes edge with evidence_type require; `inherits` gives an inherits edge (ast_extends); an undeclared class gets a dst minted by make_symbol_id. 20 tests. Behaviour change: resources inside a namespaced class get new stable_ids (the class is now extracted). Live repro on merged dev, a multi-line m.pp: class a::b {}, class c {}, class d inherits c {}, class top { include a::b, c / include \"c\" / require d / include missing::thing }. `hypergumbo survey pp2` rc=0 -> classes [a::b, c, d, top]; inherits d -> c (ast_extends, real dst); includes -> a::b (include), -> c (include, once), -> d (require), all real dsts; -> missing::thing (include) to a minted external_symbol. Before: a::b not a class, `c` from the list and the quoted \"c\" dropped. Residual, filed separately: include/require edges still start at the manifest FILE, not the enclosing class (documented design before and after this PR)."  # 8a69
